# ── Audit build ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loaded by `vite build --mode audit`, which lighthouse_audit.mjs serves.
#
# Why a file and not inline env vars: Git Bash rewrites POSIX-looking values
# on their way to a child process, so `VITE_BASE=/ npx vite build` baked
# /Program Files/Git/ into every asset URL — the page then loaded zero
# scripts and Lighthouse reported NO_FCP, which reads like a performance
# disaster rather than a quoting accident. .env.production carries the same
# warning for the same reason.
#
# Differences from .env.production, and why:
#   VITE_BASE=/            served at the origin root, not /pawsmarket/
#   VITE_HASH_ROUTER=false clean paths, so the audit measures /explore
#                          rather than /#/explore
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=     empty, so the app calls same-origin /api/* and
#                          serve_dist.mjs proxies it to the local backend
VITE_BASE=/
VITE_HASH_ROUTER=false
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
